// The board: the rules, the bots, and every pixel of the game that is not text.
//
// One sprite draws the whole board with the pen — 64 tiles, then the tints, the
// move markers and the pieces — by pointing at a square, switching costume and
// stamping. There is no clone anywhere in the project: a redraw is a few hundred
// stamps inside one warp procedure, so it lands in a single frame and leaves no
// state behind, and a piece at rest is a costume rather than a sprite to keep in
// step with the board.
//
// The pen cannot see a click, a drag or a hover, so the board does not ask it
// to. It samples the mouse in its own forever loop and works out which square or
// which button is under the pointer itself.
//
// A piece that moves is the exception: it is this sprite. The pen has one layer
// for the whole stage and clearing it would clear the panel too, so a flight
// stamps nothing at all — the piece is left out of the board's pieces, the
// sprite puts its costume on and the renderer draws it above the ink, at the
// position a second order system integrates. That position is the state rather
// than a keyframe curve: it carries its velocity into a new goal, so a piece can
// be retargeted mid-flight by picking it up again, and a frame too long to be
// stable is subdivided. Dragging sets the goal to the pointer and dropping sets
// it to the square. The move ends by stamping the board once more, with the
// piece back on its square, and going back to being a pen.

use engine;
use sprites::pieces;
use sprites::theme;
use layout;

sprite "Board" {
    costume "blank" = "assets/blank.svg";
    costume "sq-light" = "assets/sq-light.svg";
    costume "sq-dark" = "assets/sq-dark.svg";
    costume "bs0l" = "assets/bs0l.svg";
    costume "bs0d" = "assets/bs0d.svg";
    costume "bs1l" = "assets/bs1l.svg";
    costume "bs1d" = "assets/bs1d.svg";
    costume "bs2l" = "assets/bs2l.svg";
    costume "bs2d" = "assets/bs2d.svg";
    costume "bs3l" = "assets/bs3l.svg";
    costume "bs3d" = "assets/bs3d.svg";
    costume "hl-last" = "assets/hl-last.svg";
    costume "hl-sel" = "assets/hl-sel.svg";
    costume "hl-check" = "assets/hl-check.svg";
    costume "hl-hover" = "assets/hl-hover.svg";
    costume "dot" = "assets/dot.svg";
    costume "ring" = "assets/ring.svg";
    costume "promo-box" = "assets/promo-box.svg";
    // BEGIN PIECE COSTUMES
    // Everything between these two markers is generated by tools/assets.mjs:
    // one PNG per piece per size it is stamped at, and every one of them is
    // stamped at size 100. The board draws `p` and `d`, the panel `c` and
    // `s`; all four are here because `pieces.rav` names them all and a module
    // is compiled into every target that uses it. Do not edit it by hand.
    // 36 units: p<set><piece>
    // 40 units: d<set><piece>
    // 24 units: c<set><piece>
    // 22 units: s<set><piece>
    costume "p0wP" = "assets/p0wP.png";
    costume "d0wP" = "assets/d0wP.png";
    costume "c0wP" = "assets/c0wP.png";
    costume "s0wP" = "assets/s0wP.png";
    costume "p0wN" = "assets/p0wN.png";
    costume "d0wN" = "assets/d0wN.png";
